                <pb facs="0679" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.1 Polk, Frank L.:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-05T22:00:00+01:00">September 5, 1919—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4061. Strictly confidential for the Secretary of State from Polk. Your 3019,
                    September 3. Very many thanks. Quite understand the situation and will follow
                    your advice. I do not look for the slightest friction now. Polk.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
